  <name>CataMount</name>
  <summary>Map SMB and NFS network drives</summary>
  <developer id="com.spazcat">
    <name>Spazcat Enterprises</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      CataMount works like “Map network drive” on Windows. Pick an SMB or NFS share,
      choose a local folder, and CataMount creates a persistent systemd mount that
      reconnects at startup or on first access.
    </p>
    <p>
      It never edits /etc/fstab and shows existing fstab network mounts read-only.
    </p>
  </description>
